/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Pascal's law says pressure applied to a trapped liquid is transmitted equally in all directions.
   - F is force in newtons (N); p is pressure in pascals (Pa); A is piston area in square metres (m²).
   - Pressure is not force.
   - In an open-centre system the pump output can return to the reservoir at low pressure when no user needs flow.
   - The supply chain is reservoir → pumps → filter → accumulator → selector valve → actuator → return.
   - An engine-driven pump is the main source in flight.
   - A relief valve opens to return when pressure exceeds a set limit.
   - Filters sit on the pressure and return lines.
   - Transport aircraft carry two or three independent systems, each with its own reservoir, pumps and users: green, blue and yellow on the A320 family, left, centre and right on many Boeing types.
   - In normal mode the main pump supplies all users.
*/
