/* book exam traps: Do not write that bleed air normally comes from the HP stage. The HP port feeds the system only at low engine power; at cruise and climb power the LP port is enough and the HP valve stays closed. | Using gauge pressure instead of absolute pressure in ρ = p/(RT). The formula needs absolute pressure in Pa and absolute temperature in K. | Thinking the isolation valve is a check valve. A check valve is one-way and automatic; an isolation valve is opened or closed by command to split the manifold. | A duct overheat or leak closes the bleed and isolation valves for that section, not the pack valve alone; the pack valve only stops flow into one pack. | Use absolute pressure in p₁V₁ = p₂V₂ and in ρ = p/(RT); with gauge values the answer is wrong, most of all at low pressure. */
